WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.525
The inventory lists every screenshot the docs use. Both of ours were captured for P1 0.16.0.

00:07.505 --> 00:21.380
Release check compares the SDK installed in the capture app with the latest published version. The app runs 0.16.0, and 0.20.0 is out, so it warns you to update the app before capturing.

00:21.360 --> 00:29.610
Checking against 0.20.0 flags both screenshots as behind, and prints the exact command that retargets each one.

00:29.590 --> 00:35.065
Approving a screenshot for 0.20.0 tells the capture step to shoot it again.

00:35.045 --> 00:37.570
Same for the workstream selector.

00:37.550 --> 00:45.250
Both records are now approved for 0.20.0, marked refresh. Nothing is captured until a person approves it.
